# STAGE A — Contracts + parallel plumbing (no gameplay change)

**Prompt**

> You are working in an existing deterministic JS sim with timeline replay + time travel.
> Non-negotiable invariants:
>
> * Do not change gameplay behavior in this stage.
> * Determinism suite must pass exactly as before.
> * No changes that affect timeline replay/projection semantics.
>
> Objective:
>
> * Introduce the new board + defs contracts in parallel (dual-write/dual-read), and render the new 12-column rows from the new board state.
>
> Required design contracts:
>
> 1. Add `state.board` as the canonical home for the new system:
>
>    * `board.width = 12`
>    * `board.env.tilesById`, `board.env.cardsById`
>    * `board.city.permanentsById`
>    * derived occupancy arrays: `tileOcc`, `cardOcc`, `permOcc` (NOT serialized)
>    * `board.cadence = { intervalSec, lastTickSec, nextTickSec, alignToSeasonStart?, seasonAnchorSec? }`
>    * add id counters: `nextEnvTileInstanceId`, `nextEnvCardInstanceId`
> 2. Implement `rebuildBoardDerived(state)`:
>
>    * deterministic rebuild of occupancy arrays from instances’ `{col, span}`
>    * detect overlaps and resolve deterministically by “last writer wins” OR log warning but keep stable output (pick one and document)
> 3. Serialization rules:
>
>    * strip derived occupancy arrays on serialize (like inventory grid)
>    * rebuild derived occupancy arrays on deserialize
> 4. Defs (placeholder content only, not referenced by sim yet):
>
>    * Add `EnvTileDefs` with 8–12 placeholder tiles including per-season weighted `seasonTables`
>    * Add `EnvEventDefs` with 15–30 placeholder events; include a few AddResource effects but DO NOT wire spawning yet
> 5. Scenario/init:
>
>    * Populate `state.board` with an initial tile layout (12 columns, mostly span=1)
>    * Populate `state.board.city.permanentsById` from existing scenario placements (mirror existing permanents; don’t remove legacy permanentSlots yet)
> 6. Views:
>
>    * Update board rendering to draw:
>
>      * env tiles row from `state.board`
>      * env events row (empty for now)
>      * permanent row from `state.board` (or mirrored mapping)
>    * Keep legacy envSlots/permanentSlots logic intact; do not delete old rendering until stage C.
>
> Constraints:
>
> * No cadence spawning logic in this stage.
> * No behavior/effect changes that could alter simulation outcomes.
> * Keep old envSlots/envSeasons fully functional.
> * Prefer additive changes and dual-read fallbacks where needed.
>
> Deliverables:
>
> * Modified/added files with full code.
> * A short “how to smoke test” list:
>
>   1. run determinism suite
>   2. run app, verify 3 aligned 12-column rows render
>   3. scrub timegraph briefly (no new behavior expected)
>
> Acceptance criteria:
>
> * Determinism suite passes.
> * No runtime errors.
> * New board rows render without affecting gameplay.

